              {
                "text": "**Analyzing the Grid Division**\n\nI've got a handle on how the grid's being split. Specifically, train 1's 11x11 grid is divided by a line of 5s at row 5. The top half is rows 0-4; bottom half is 6-10. Output dims are 5x11. I see it now.\n\n\n**Investigating the Combination Logic**\n\nOkay, I'm digging into how the top and bottom halves merge. It seems the bottom half's values are overwriting the top half when they share a position. For example, (1,1) has a 2 in the top and a 3 in the bottom, and the output shows a 3. I'm checking this consistently in train 1, and now train 3, examining the divider line and how top/bottom elements interact. So far, it's seeming like the bottom half does overwrites!\n\n\n**Clarifying the Overwrite Rule**\n\nI'm starting to grasp this overlay logic. It's not just top/bottom or left/right; the second grid half *always* overlays the first, and where they overlap, the second half's non-background pixels overwrite the first's. I'm focusing on why, and working through the trains to determine which value is the background. I think I'm close to an \"aha!\" moment.\n\n\n",
